**Apparent Subject:**  
A classified U.S. Department of Defense (DoD) report summarizing evidence related to Unidentified Anomalous Phenomena (UAP), Technologies of Unknown Origin (TUO), and Non-Human Intelligence (NHI). The document alleges a long-standing conspiracy within the U.S. Executive Branch to conceal UAP-related information from Congress and the public.

**Genre:**  
This work appears to be a whistleblower-style investigative report, blending elements of intelligence analysis, congressional oversight documentation, and speculative disclosure. It is presented in a formal, technical tone, with structured data tables and case-specific descriptions.

**Main Ideas:**  
The report details observations of UAPs from U.S. military and intelligence sensors, including infrared, full-motion video, and signals intelligence. It categorizes UAP shapes (e.g., spheres, discs, boomerangs, triangles) and describes anomalous behaviors such as silent flight, sudden acceleration, and electromagnetic interference. The author claims that the DoD has withheld critical information about UAPs from Congress for years, including the existence of special access programs (SAPs) and compartmented access programs (CAPs) tied to UAP research. The report also references support for claims made by whistleblower Lue Elizondo regarding Advanced Aerospace Threat Identification Program (AATIP) activities.

**Striking Details:**  
